course: dictionary
lesson: 4138
title: Globe: a model, a world, a light
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. «A globe is a small round model of the Earth that shows the true shapes of the lands and seas.» Here the clues are model, Earth and shapes, so a globe is a model, not a light.
explain: Look for phrases too. «Around the globe» means all over the world, and «snow globe» names a ball with water and glitter inside. In Australia and New Zealand, «turn on the globe» means switch on the light bulb.
explain: Test your choice by swapping in your meaning. If the sentence still makes sense, you probably chose well.
fact: A globe is a ball-shaped model of the Earth, with a map of the world on it.
fact: «Around the globe» means all over the world, or the whole Earth.
fact: Any object shaped like a ball can be called a globe, such as a «snow globe».
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, a globe can mean a light bulb.
fact: A globe shows the Earth's real shape more accurately than a flat map, which stretches some places.
exercise: «A globe is a small round model of the Earth that shows the true shapes of the lands and seas.» What is a globe in this sentence? | A kind of sea | A light bulb | A flat map of one country | *A small round model of the Earth
exercise: Dad says, «We will fly around the globe this summer.» What does globe mean here? | A small ball | A light bulb | *The whole world | A snow globe
exercise: In Sydney, Tom says, «Turn on the globe, it's dark.» What does globe mean here? | A round ball of wool | *A light bulb | A snow globe | A model of the Earth
test: What does a globe show better than a flat map? | Only the colour of the sea | A list of the tallest mountains only | *The true shapes of lands and seas, without stretching | The weather for next week
test: «Look at a globe from below and you see mostly blue.» Why is there so much blue? | The globe is made of water | *Oceans cover about 71 percent of the Earth | The paint is blue | Blue is the Earth's favourite colour
exam: Which phrase means all over the world? | *Around the globe | A globe lamp in the kitchen | A snow globe | Spin the paint
